{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's props and emitted events."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-inputs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text inputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many Vue components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelValue"},{"type":"text","value":" and emit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update:modelValue"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name=\"name\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <TextInput\n    :name=\"field.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    :model-value=\"field.value\"\n    :error=\"field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the current value rather than a one-time default so the UI remains driven\nby form state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checkboxes and switches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapt the event used by the component library:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <Checkbox\n    :checked=\"field.value\"\n    :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:checked=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | 'indeterminate'"},{"type":"text","value":". Normalize it at the boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Checkbox\n  :checked=\"field.value\"\n  @update:checked=\"(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)\"\n/>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<DatePicker\n  :model-value=\"field.value\"\n  @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n/>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reuse-the-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse the adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a component\nwhose props include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FieldWithValue<T>"},{"type":"text","value":", then register it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen it should be available as a typed app field component."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The repository's Vue large-form example demonstrates\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFormHookHelpers"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFormHook"},{"type":"text","value":", injected app fields, and a reusable\nfield group."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"text-inputs","text":"Text inputs","level":2},{"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","text":"Checkboxes and switches","level":2},{"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","text":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls","level":2},{"id":"reuse-the-adapter","text":"Reuse the adapter","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's props and emitted events.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nMany Vue components use `modelValue` and emit `update:modelValue`:\n\n```vue\n<form.Field name=\"name\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <TextInput\n    :name=\"field.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    :model-value=\"field.value\"\n    :error=\"field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nPass the current value rather than a one-time default so the UI remains driven\nby form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nAdapt the event used by the component library:\n\n```vue\n<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <Checkbox\n    :checked=\"field.value\"\n    :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:checked=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize it at the boundary:\n\n```vue\n<Checkbox\n  :checked=\"field.value\"\n  @update:checked=\"(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```vue\n<DatePicker\n  :model-value=\"field.value\"\n  @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a component\nwhose props include `FieldWithValue<T>`, then register it with `createFormHook`\nwhen it should be available as a typed app field component.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's Vue large-form example demonstrates\n`getFormHookHelpers`, `createFormHook`, injected app fields, and a reusable\nfield group.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ui-libraries\ntitle: UI Libraries\n---\n\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's props and emitted events.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nMany Vue components use `modelValue` and emit `update:modelValue`:\n\n```vue\n<form.Field name=\"name\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <TextInput\n    :name=\"field.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    :model-value=\"field.value\"\n    :error=\"field.errors.map((error) => error.message).join(', ')\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nPass the current value rather than a one-time default so the UI remains driven\nby form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nAdapt the event used by the component library:\n\n```vue\n<form.Field name=\"acceptedTerms\" v-slot=\"{ field }\">\n  <Checkbox\n    :checked=\"field.value\"\n    :aria-invalid=\"field.meta.isInvalid\"\n    @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n    @update:checked=\"field.handleChange\"\n  />\n</form.Field>\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize it at the boundary:\n\n```vue\n<Checkbox\n  :checked=\"field.value\"\n  @update:checked=\"(checked) => field.handleChange(checked === true)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.handleChange`:\n\n```vue\n<DatePicker\n  :model-value=\"field.value\"\n  @update:model-value=\"field.handleChange\"\n  @blur=\"field.handleBlur\"\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nIf the same wiring appears throughout the application, extract a component\nwhose props include `FieldWithValue<T>`, then register it with `createFormHook`\nwhen it should be available as a typed app field component.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's Vue large-form example demonstrates\n`getFormHookHelpers`, `createFormHook`, injected app fields, and a reusable\nfield group.\n"}
